From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KadirJeager <KadirJeager@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] input: hall_logical: report tablet mode while no keyboard is
 attached

The desktop framework does not decide between laptop and tablet from
the input devices alone. Its device state provider maps SW_TABLET_MODE
and SW_LID onto CLOSED, OPEN and TABLET, and the window manager keeps
the desktop (freeform) layout in OPEN even with no keyboard or
touchpad. hall_logical cleared SW_TABLET_MODE when the keyboard was
detached, so a bare tablet stayed in the laptop state, while folding
the cover back reached the tablet state.

Report SW_TABLET_MODE whenever no keyboard cover is attached, the same
as other detachables do (cros_cbas, surface tabletsw). hall_logical
now follows ATTACHED as well as DETACHED; both are replayed on
registration once the pogo driver knows the connection state. Until
ATTACHED arrives, including a boot without a keyboard, where the pogo
driver sends nothing, the device is a slate. SW_LID still follows the
attached cover only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/keyboard/hall_ic_logical.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/keyboard/hall_ic_logical.c b/drivers/input/keyboard/hall_ic_logical.c
index efdc9d3a9..08f75041a 100644
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/hall_ic_logical.c
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/hall_ic_logical.c
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ struct hall_drvdata {
 };
 
 static int hall_logical_status = 0;
+/* A keyboard cover is attached; false until the pogo driver says so. */
+static bool hall_logical_attached;
 
 static ssize_t hall_logical_detect_show(struct device *dev,
 				struct device_attribute *attr, char *buf)
@@ -56,19 +58,23 @@ static ssize_t hall_logical_detect_show(struct device *dev,
 static DEVICE_ATTR(hall_logical_detect, 0444, hall_logical_detect_show, NULL);
 
 /*
- * The logical hall state maps onto two standard switches:
- *   CLOSE (cover over the screen)   -> SW_LID = 1
- *   BACK  (cover folded behind it)  -> SW_TABLET_MODE = 1
- *   OPEN  (laptop position, or no cover attached) -> both 0
+ * The cover state maps onto two standard switches:
+ *   CLOSE (cover over the screen)                 -> SW_LID = 1
+ *   BACK  (cover folded behind it), or no cover   -> SW_TABLET_MODE = 1
+ *   OPEN  (laptop position)                       -> both 0
+ * Without a keyboard the device is a slate, as on other detachables
+ * (cros_cbas, surface tabletsw): the desktop framework derives its
+ * device state from SW_TABLET_MODE and stays in the laptop state while
+ * it is 0, whether or not a keyboard is present.
  * The stock driver reports the folded-back state with the vendor switch
  * SW_HALL_LOGICAL that only the vendor framework understands;
  * SW_TABLET_MODE is the switch Android's InputManager tracks.
  */
 static void hall_logical_report(struct input_dev *input)
 {
-	input_report_switch(input, SW_LID,
+	input_report_switch(input, SW_LID, hall_logical_attached &&
 			hall_logical_status == LOGICAL_HALL_CLOSE);
-	input_report_switch(input, SW_TABLET_MODE,
+	input_report_switch(input, SW_TABLET_MODE, !hall_logical_attached ||
 			hall_logical_status == LOGICAL_HALL_BACK);
 	input_sync(input);
 }
@@ -98,8 +104,19 @@ static int logical_hallic_notifier_handler(struct notifier_block *nb,
 	struct pogo_data_struct pogo_data =  *(struct pogo_data_struct *)data;
 	int hall_status;
 
+	/*
+	 * ATTACHED and DETACHED are also replayed on registration once the
+	 * pogo driver knows the connection state. Before that, and when no
+	 * keyboard is found at boot, nothing is sent and the device stays a
+	 * slate.
+	 */
 	switch (action) {
+	case POGO_NOTIFIER_ID_ATTACHED:
+		hall_logical_attached = true;
+		hall_logical_report(logical_hall_dev->input);
+		break;
 	case POGO_NOTIFIER_ID_DETACHED:
+		hall_logical_attached = false;
 		hall_logical_status = LOGICAL_HALL_OPEN;
 		hall_logical_report(logical_hall_dev->input);
 		break;
